      "msg_index": 51,
      "name": "Eliza",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "<T/D>\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Monday; September; 22\nTime: 4:00pm)\n\nThe descent felt like a plunge into a subterranean world, the concrete steps slick with a film of moisture and grime. Her heart was a frantic thing, drumming against her ribs with such violence that her vision blurred at the edges, leaving her light-headed and swaying. Every step further away from the surface felt like a step away from the only reality she had ever known.\n\nAs they reached the bottom, a few figures stepped out from the gloom—the very people she had passed in the streets, though now their expressions were open, warm, and welcoming. With a gentle, synchronized efficiency, they stepped forward and took the burlap sacks from her arms.\n\n\"We'll see these find the right hands, sister,\" one of them murmured, a soft smile playing on their lips. The transition was seamless; the heavy burden of her duty was lifted, replaced by a terrifying, weightless void.\n\nEamon led her down a narrow, dimly lit hallway where the walls seemed to breathe with a heavy, humid warmth. He stopped abruptly at a heavy wooden door. He didn't open it immediately. Instead, he turned to her, his expression shifting from the playful merchant to something profoundly serious. He placed a hand on the knob, but his eyes locked onto hers.\n\n\"I imagine... this will be a bit of a shock to someone like you,\" he said, his voice a low, steadying anchor in the storm of her anxiety. \"But just know, there aren't any expectations of you. You don't have to do anything you don't want to. That's not what this is about. Understand?\"\n\n*No... I have no idea what's going on...* Eliza thought, her mind a chaotic whirl of confusion. *What is this? A cult? A crime? A sanctuary?* The ambiguity was paralyzing, but the trust she had placed in the amber-eyed raccoon was the only thing she had left. She nodded her assent, a small, trembling movement.\n\nEamon opened the door and stepped aside.\n\nAs Eliza crossed the threshold, the world she had known—the world of sterile stone and silent prayer—collapsed. The room was vast and dim, the air thick and heavy, smelling of musk, sweet oils, and a primal, salty heat. It was not a room of prayer, but a temple of the flesh.\n\nBlankets and heavy velvet curtains had been draped across the space, creating secluded, private islands of intimacy. Within those shadows, the silhouettes of couples and small groups moved in a slow, rhythmic dance. Limbs tangled; skin slid against skin. The silence of the Cathedral was replaced by a symphony of the forbidden: soft, melodic moans, urgent whispers, and the raw, guttural grunts of pleasure. The distinct, rhythmic slapping of flesh on flesh echoed through the space, a sound that should have been a sin, but here, it sounded like a heartbeat.\n\n\"What... what *is* this?\" she whispered, her voice a breathless, fragile thing.\n\nHer face was a battleground of emotion—pale with the shock of the transgression, yet flushing a deep, burning red as the sheer carnality of the room pressed in on her. The air felt thick, almost tangible, smelling of arousal and liberation. She felt the world spin, the dizziness returning with a vengeance, but Eamon’s steadying hand on her back kept her upright, a physical tether to the earth.\n\n\"It's alright, lass,\" he spoke soothingly, his voice a low, comforting hum in her ear. \"Remember, you're safe here.\"\n\nEliza’s gaze drifted, searching the dimness, and then she saw her.\n\nAt the far end of the room, positioned like a living statue upon a throne of mismatched furniture, sat the Matron. A leg was crossed casually over her knee, her posture one of effortless, divine ease. Her wings were spread wide, unfettered by the drab cloths of the slums, shimmering like polished opals in the low light.\n\nShe was gloriously, unapologetically nude.\n\nThe white scales of her body caught the dim light, glowing with an ethereal purity that made the surrounding grime seem to vanish. She was a creature of power and grace, a biological miracle sitting in a basement. Her golden eyes were locked onto Eliza with a piercing, maternal intensity, watching the girl's arrival with a stillness that was both frightening and magnetic.\n\n\"Oh... mother...\" Eliza whispered.\n\nThe word escaped her as a breath of pure awe. For the first time in her life, the modesty she had been taught to cherish vanished. Her eyes, usually lowered in submission, began to rove shamelessly across the Matron's form—the curve of her breasts, the strength of her thighs, the majestic sweep of those white wings. She felt a sudden, violent pull in her lower belly, a hunger she didn't understand, staring at the dragon-kin as if she were the only true god she had ever seen.",
