ngers dug into Verali's shoulders, her nails scratching lightly against the white scales. She was trembling, her entire body shaking with the effort of processing the sensation. For a moment, the pain and the pleasure were indistinguishable—a single, roaring white noise of feeling.\n\nBut then, the friction took over.\n\nAs Verali began to move, a slow, rhythmic slide that synchronized with the thumping of the warehouse's distant lovers, Eliza's expression shifted. The shock faded, replaced by a look of sheer, transcendent wonder. She arched her back, her chest heaving, her head falling back as she let out a long, melodic moan—a sound of pure, unadulterated release.\n\nIt was the sound of a thousand prayers being answered, not by a silent goddess in a stained-glass window, but by the living, breathing warmth of another person.\n\nThe rhythm accelerated, driven by the shared hunger and the lingering power of the gold seed. The friction became a fire, the heat an inferno. Eliza's movements became more frantic, her hips rising to meet Verali's, her breath coming in short, jagged bursts of \"please\" and \"more.\"\n\nThey were no longer an acolyte and a Matron; they were two animals in a dark room, stripped of title and rank, reduced to the most honest version of themselves. Verali felt the tension in Eliza's muscles reach a breaking point, a sudden, violent shuddering that rippled through the girl's entire frame.\n\nEliza's eyes snapped shut, her face contorting in a mask of exquisite agony as she reached her peak. It wasn't the quiet, controlled release the Church might have described in its warnings about \"the leak\"; it was a total collapse. A spiritual and physical surrender that left her limp, her voice a broken whisper of Verali's name.\n\nMoments later, Verali followed her, a guttural growl escaping her throat as she surrendered to the tide.\n\nThe silence that returned to the closet was heavy and thick, broken only by the sound of their synchronized, ragged breathing. They lay tangled together, the mattress beneath them damp and smelling of salt and musk. The adrenaline began to recede, replaced by a profound, heavy exhaustion.\n\nVerali didn't pull away. She stayed wrapped around Eliza, her wings shielding the girl from the draft of the room, her heart beating a slow, steady rhythm against Eliza's ear. For a long time, neither of them spoke. There was nothing left to say. The void had been filled, and for the first time in her life, Eliza felt completely, utterly full.",
