    "2026-05-12T03:53:37.390Z": {
      "msg_index": 64,
      "name": "Eliza",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "<T/D>\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Monday; September; 22\nTime: 6:00pm)\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Monday; September; 22\nTime: 4:00pm)\n\n\nThe cocoon of Verali's wings felt like the only safe place left in the world. Wrapped in that ivory warmth, Eliza felt a heavy, shimmering peace, her mind floating in a haze of post-coital bliss. She didn't want the world to start again. She wanted to stay here, suspended in the golden amber of the moment, where the only law was the beat of Verali's heart against her own.\n\nBut the world, as it always did, came knocking.\n\nA soft, tentative rap sounded against the wooden door of the utility closet—a sharp contrast to the primal sounds that had filled the room moments before. Eamon’s voice drifted through the gaps in the door, low and cautious, carrying a note of gentle urgency.\n\n\"I'm terribly sorry to bother you, Matron... Sister... but the hour is getting on. The shadows are stretching, and the eyes of the city are turning back toward the Cathedral.\"\n\nThe words were a cold splash of water. The meaning was crystal clear: the window of safety had closed. Eliza had been gone for as long as was safe; every minute she remained was a minute that increased the likelihood of a missing-person report, a suspicious check by a Warden, or a panicked inquiry from Cecilia.\n\nEliza stiffened, her heart giving a sudden, anxious leap. She didn't want to go. She clung fiercely to Verali for a few final moments, her fingers digging into the white scales as if she could somehow anchor herself to the Matron's body and stay forever. She felt the abrupt return of the cold air as Verali’s wings slowly unfurled, exposing her to the dampness of the closet once more.\n\nWith a long-suffering sigh and a groan that hinted at a pleasant, heavy soreness between her legs—a physical reminder of what she had just surrendered—Eliza peeled herself away.\n\nThe process of dressing was a slow, agonizing regression. Each piece of clothing felt like a layer of the mask being reapplied. As she pulled on her undergarments, she felt the sticky, warm trace of Verali's seed, a secret she would carry back into the heart of the beast. When she slid back into the heavy black-and-white habit, the coarse wool felt scratchy and oppressive, a stark contrast to the skin-to-skin heat she had just known. She felt like she was being entombed in her own piety.\n\nBefore they stepped out, Verali leaned down. The dragon-kin’s presence was imposing, her muscular frame filling the room, but her movement was tender. She pressed her lips to Eliza's in a final, lingering kiss.\n\n\"Stay safe,\" Verali whispered, her voice shy and quiet, a soft fragility that sat at odds with her towering stature and her role as the cell's divine anchor. \"Don't take any foolish risks... I... I very much want to see you again.\"\n\nEliza looked up at her, her light-blue eyes shimmering. In that moment, Verali wasn't just a Matron or a savior; she was the center of Eliza's universe.\n\n\"The High Inquisitor himself couldn't keep me from you,\" Eliza replied, her voice breathless and certain. It was the most defiant thing she had ever said.\n\nShe wrapped Verali in one last, tight hug, squeezing the Matron as if she were trying to memorize the feel of her scales through her robes. Then, with a final, lingering look, she stepped out of the closet and back into the main room.\n\nThis time, the warehouse was different. The sight of the tangled lovers, the raw sounds of pleasure, and the musk of the sanctuary no longer felt like a vertigo-inducing shock. Instead, it felt natural—familiar. She walked through the dim space with a new kind of confidence, her steps a little slower, her gaze a little more open. She was no longer a spectator to the liberation; she was a part of it.\n\nAs she reached the exit, she caught Eamon studying her face. The raccoon merchant's amber eyes were knowing, reading the flush in her cheeks and the soft, dazed look in her eyes like an open book.\n\nEliza felt a surge of heat climb her neck. She blushed and glanced away with an embarrassed, small smile, a tiny, private laugh bubbling in her chest. She knew exactly what he saw.\n\n\"I'm ready,\" she said, her voice soft but steady, spoken to nobody in particular.\n\nEamon gave a sharp, respectful nod to Verali, then stepped beside Eliza, his presence a steadying guide as he escorted her back out into the bitter cold of the city.",
