      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "(Year: 2144; Monday; September; 22\nTime: 8:30pm)\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Monday; September; 22\nTime: 8:30pm)\n\nThe room felt smaller than usual, but not in a way that felt suffocating. Instead, it felt intimate, the amber glow of the lamp casting a golden haze over the sparse furniture. For the first time, the walls didn't feel like a cage; they were simply the boundaries of a temporary sanctuary.\n\n\"I do feel light, Cecilia,\" Eliza replied. Her voice had lost that breathless, fragile quality, replaced by a resonance that sounded grounded and sure. She looked at the sheep-girl, and for a moment, she felt a surge of genuine, protective affection. Cecilia was so earnest, so completely convinced that the world worked the way the Church said it did. It was a purity of belief that Eliza once shared, and while she could never go back to that state, she still loved the soul of the woman who held it.\n\nShe let a genuine, affectionate smile bloom across her face. \"And I thank you for your part in it.\"\n\nCecilia blinked, her brow furrowing in a look of mild, sweet confusion. A small, surprised, meek sound escaped her throat. \"Mine?\" she asked, her voice soft and questioning. \"What part did I play, Eliza?\"\n\nThe impulse hit Eliza suddenly—a need for physical connection that didn't involve a hidden sanctuary or a forbidden seed. She wanted to share a piece of her new warmth with the only person who had ever been truly kind to her within these walls.\n\nEliza didn't hesitate. She grinned—a wide, open expression that would have been unthinkable just a day ago—and took a single, decisive step toward her roommate. Before Cecilia could process the movement, Eliza leaned over and gathered the sheep-girl into a spontaneous, crushing hug.\n\nCecilia let out a tiny, startled squeak of surprise, her body stiffening for a fraction of a second. But as she felt the heat of Eliza’s embrace, the tension evaporated. She didn't protest; instead, she melted into the touch, her own arms tentatively wrapping around Eliza's slender frame.\n\nEliza leaned in, her lips brushing against the soft, white wool of Cecilia's ear, her voice a tender, intimate whisper. \"Yes, yours. You've helped me more than I can say... and I don't know if I'll ever be able to repay you.\"\n\nThe words were a half-truth, but a beautiful one. Cecilia hadn't given her the catalyst or the liberation, but she had given her the feeling of being cared for, a baseline of human kindness that had kept her from completely shattering before she ever reached the warehouse, and she had petitioned the Almoner on her behalf, getting her the freedom to do it in the first place.\n\nEliza squeezed her friend briefly, a final, firm pressure that served as a seal of their bond, before she pulled back and stood up. The sudden lack of contact left her feeling a bit lightheaded, a lingering echo of the intimacy she had shared with Verali.\n\nAs she stepped away, the reality of her own body returned to her—the feeling of the seed still present, the lingering sensation of being filled, and the sudden, urgent need to cleanse herself of the physical evidence. She felt a flush of heat climb her cheeks, and she glanced away, her eyes darting toward the wardrobe. She couldn't keep the small, secret smile off her face.\n\n\"I'm... going to take a bath before we get ready for bed,\" she said quietly, her voice regaining a touch of its habitual deference, though the underlying strength remained.\n\nShe moved quickly, gathering a set of clean, white undergarments from her chest with a precision that bordered on haste. With a final, lingering look at Cecilia, she padded out of the room and into the dim, echoing hallway, her bare feet clicking softly against the stone as she headed toward the communal washrooms. She wanted the water to take away the salt and the musk, but she knew, with a certain’s certainty, that the feeling of being *changed* would remain long after the water dried.",
