      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "<T/D>\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Wednesday; September; 24\nTime: 1:30pm)\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Wednesday; September; 24\nTime: 1:45pm)\n\n\nCecilia stared at her, her brow furrowing. The change in Eliza was palpable—a transformation that happened in the space of a single afternoon. The girl who had always been a mirror of Cecilia's own piety, the one who had lived and breathed the same conditioned air, had suddenly become something... different. She looked at Eliza and didn't see a ghost anymore. She saw someone who had found a secret door and walked through it.\n\n*\"I've made my peace with Father Gaspard.\"*\n\nThe words sounded wrong. You didn't make peace with a predator; you survived him, or you were consumed by him. There was no middle ground, no peaceful coexistence with a man who viewed you as a prize. Yet, as Cecilia looked at the enigmatic smile on Eliza's face, she realized that Eliza wasn't talking about a truce. She was talking about a victory.\n\n\"I don't understand,\" Cecilia whispered, her voice small and unhurried. \"How can you not be scared? He's... he's the Examiner. He can say anything about us. He can tell the Mother we've sinned, and we'd have no way to prove otherwise.\"\n\nShe looked down at their joined hands, the contrast between them striking—Eliza’s grip steady and sure, her own trembling. The \"duty\" Eliza mentioned felt like a heavy chain, but the way Eliza spoke of it sounded more like a costume.\n\nA sudden, sharp realization hit Cecilia. She remembered the way Eliza had looked at the dragon-kin in the market—not with the disgust the Church taught, but with a profound, aching recognition. She remembered the way Eliza had spoken of the \"holiness of the self.\"\n\n\"Eliza...\" Cecilia's voice dropped to a barely audible breath, her brown eyes wide with a sudden, terrifying curiosity. \"Did something... *happen*? While you were out? When you were away from the Cathedral?\"\n\nShe didn't know how to ask the question—she had no vocabulary for rebellion, no words for the 'Contamination' that wasn't a slur. But she could feel it. There was a scent of something different on Eliza, a vibration of energy that didn't belong in the sterile halls of the residential block. It was as if Eliza had come back from the slums with a piece of the world clinging to her.\n\n\"You're different,\" Cecilia whispered, her voice trembling. \"You're not... you're not pretending anymore, are you?\"\n\nShe didn't pull her hand away. Instead, she squeezed tighter, her heart hammering against her ribs. For the first time in her life, Cecilia found herself longing for the truth, no matter how dangerous it was. She wanted to know what Eliza had found in the dark, because the light of the Cathedral had suddenly started to feel like a blinding, oppressive glare.",
