tled, the atmosphere in the leather loft shifted. The tenderness of the afterglow was incinerated by a sudden, scorching heat. Verali felt a roar building in her chest, a physical vibration that made the leather bales around them shudder.\n\n*A predator in a priest's robe,* Verali thought, her claws involuntarily extending, digging deep into the soft leather of the nest. *He uses the law of the goddess to hunt the girls he's supposed to protect.*\n\nThe fury was a living thing. It wasn't just anger; it was a righteous, shimmering hatred. The thought of Gaspard’s hands on Eliza—the hands of a man who bragged about rigging a biological lottery to satisfy his own appetites—made Verali’s scales itch with a need for violence.\n\nShe didn't pull away from Eliza; instead, she pulled her closer, her embrace becoming a shield. Verali's wings snapped shut around them, creating a dark, private cocoon that shut out the light of the loft.\n\n\"He will not touch you,\" Verali hissed, the words vibrating with a lethal intensity. \"I do not care what laws he writes or what lotteries he rigs. He is a worm, Eliza. A parasite pretending to be a shepherd.\"\n\nVerali leaned back just enough to look Eliza in the eyes, her gaze burning with a fierce, protective fire. \"You are not a vessel for the Church. You are not a piece of property to be assigned. You are *mine*... and I will burn that Cathedral to the ground before I let him lay a finger on you.\"",
