      "mes": "<T/D>\n\n\n(Year: 2144; Tuesday; September; 30\nTime: 4:00pm)\n\n\nEliza huffed, a small, sharp sound of dismissal that felt entirely alien to the girl who had once bowed her head in every corridor. She shifted her weight, leaning back against the leather bales, her expression one of a cold, calculated clarity.\n\n\"He is a weak, fat, drunken coward,\" she stated, her voice devoid of its usual breathy hesitation. \"I can see that now. He hides behind the law because he has nothing else. He is a man of appetites and shadows, and as long as I remain the picture of obedience... as long as I play the part of the humble acolyte... he cannot do anything to me besides... well... what the Church sanctions.\"\n\nThe words were spoken with a chilling pragmatism. She was describing the 'mask' not as a burden, but as a tactical advantage. If she could stomach the physical violation, she could survive the man.\n\nBut then, the steel in her posture buckled. The resolve vanished, replaced by a heavy, shuddering sigh that seemed to vibrate through her entire frame. The sigh turned into a full-body shiver, her shoulders hunching as if she were suddenly cold.\n\n\"And then...\" she whispered, her voice cracking, \"Mother... I don't want to think of having to carry his child.\"\n\nThe horror of it wasn't the act itself—she had already decided she could endure the physical theft of her body—but the permanent, living evidence of that theft. The idea of a child, a piece of Gaspard's own corruption growing inside her, felt like a spiritual death sentence. It was the one thing she couldn't simply mask away.\n\nAt this, Verali tensed. The Matron’s golden eyes flared, and she sat up abruptly, her wings snapping tight against her sides. There was a sudden, fervent intensity in her gaze, as if she were desperate to offer a lifeline to a drowning person.\n\n\"That, at least, I can help with,\" Verali said, her voice ringing with a certainty that bordered on a vow.\n\nEliza froze, her blue eyes widening as she looked at the Matron with a confused, questioning gaze. \"What do you mean?\"\n\nVerali’s voice dropped, becoming quiet, almost conspiratorial, as she looked at Eliza with a flicker of distress. \"I mean... think about what we *do* here, Eliza. The nature of our cell. We are not just about liberation through pleasure; we are about the autonomy of the body.\"\n\nShe paused, her expression solemn. \"Of course we have... ways of making sure there aren't any... unwanted pregnancies. Methods of the self, catalysts that can prevent the seed from taking hold.\" Verali’s voice softened, a deep, protective warmth returning to her tone. \"Whatever that monster does to you... he won't get you pregnant. I will make sure of it.\"\n\nThe silence that followed was absolute. Eliza’s eyes widened in a look of sheer, unfiltered disbelief. For twenty-one years, the Church had taught her that reproduction was the only purpose of her existence—a biological destiny that could not be escaped, only managed by the priesthood. To hear that there was a way to *stop* it, to deny the Church its prize, was like discovering a secret door in a wall she had lived behind her entire life.\n\n\"You... you mean it?\" she whispered.\n\nWithout waiting for a second confirmation, Eliza lunged. She threw herself at Verali with a force that caught the Matron completely off guard, hugging her so tightly and with such sudden, explosive gratitude that Verali let out a startled, wheezing sound, her lungs momentarily compressed by the sheer weight of the girl's relief.\n\nThe sound broke the spell of heavy tragedy. Verali gasped, her wings fluttering in a confused, rhythmic beat, and a startled, genuine laugh escaped her throat. Eliza, hearing the Matron's struggle, began to giggle—a bright, bubbling sound that felt like the first real laugh she had ever uttered in her adult life.\n\nThey pulled back slightly, both of them breathless and laughing, the same dark shadows that had loomed over them moments ago now pushed back into the corners of the loft.\n\n\"Thank you, Verali,\" Eliza whispered, her eyes shimmering with a mixture of joy and a newfound, dangerous hope. \"You don't know how much that had been eating away at me. I... I feel like I can actually breathe now.\"",
