      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "(Year: 2144; Tuesday; September; 30\nTime: 4:00pm)\n\n\nThe laughter subsided, leaving behind a warmth that felt a hundred times more durable than the adrenaline of sex. Verali kept her arms locked around Eliza, the girl’s small, trembling frame tucked securely against the ivory expanse of her chest. She felt a profound sense of satisfaction; for the first time in this relationship, she wasn't just a catalyst for a spiritual awakening or a physical release. She had provided a concrete shield—a biological defense against a systemic horror. She felt the vibration of Eliza's relief against her skin, and it made the Matron's heart ache with a protective, maternal ferocity.\n\nThey lay there for a long time, the only sound the distant, rhythmic thumping of the tannery machinery and the soft, whistling wind of the autumn afternoon leaking through the loft's eaves. Verali’s wings remained draped over them, a heavy, cream-colored canopy that made the world feel small and safe.\n\nAs the silence deepened, Eliza stirred. She didn't pull away, but she shifted her head, her lips fluttering against the sensitive skin of Verali's neck. The touch was light, almost tentative, as if she were testing the waters of a new conversation.\n\n\"There's... something else I wanted to ask you,\" Eliza whispered, her voice muffled against the dragon-kin's scales.\n\nVerali hummed, a low, resonant sound that vibrated in her chest. She tilted her head, giving the girl more room to speak. \"I am listening, little bird. What is it?\"\n\nEliza pulled back just enough to look at her, though she remained curled in Verali's embrace. Her expression was hesitant, her blue eyes searching Verali's gold ones for a sign of approval or caution.\n\n\"It's about Cecilia,\" Eliza began, her voice gaining a bit of strength. \"My roommate. I... I've spent so much time treating her like a liability, Verali. I was afraid of her, afraid that her piety would make her a spy, or that her goodness would make her an accidental traitor.\"\n\nVerali listened in silence, her golden eyes tracking the flickering light of the lamps. She knew the nature of the acolytes—the way they were groomed to be extensions of the Church's will.\n\n\"But she's... she's different,\" Eliza continued, a small, soft smile touching her lips. \"She's started to see. She’s not just following me blindly; she’s starting to question. She’s been covering for me, supporting me... she's risked her own standing with the Church just to keep my secrets. She’s been a partner in things I didn't even realize I needed.\"\n\nEliza took a shaky breath, her fingers curling into the leather of the bale. \"I'm tired of the masks, Verali. I'm tired of pretending to her that I'm the same girl I was when we were in the creche. I don't want to keep secrets from her anymore. I want her to know... I want her to know about you. About the Testifiers.\"\n\nVerali felt a flicker of hesitation. The first rule of the cells was secrecy—compartmentalization was the only thing that kept them from being wiped out in a single night of raids. To bring an outsider in, even a trusted one, was a breach of protocol. It was a risk that could compromise the anchor, the Matron, and everyone who sought refuge.\n\nBut then she looked at Eliza. She saw the longing there—the desire for a friendship that wasn't built on a lie. She saw the way Eliza’s love for Cecilia had mirrored her own growing affection for the girl. To deny this request would be to tell Eliza that some bonds were less important than the rules of the underground.\n\nVerali let out a slow, shimmering breath. She reached out, cupping Eliza's cheek in her large, warm palm.\n\n\"If she is as you describe—if she has already chosen the truth over the mask—then she is already one of us, whether she knows it or not,\" Verali murmured, her voice a velvet, grounding current. \"The Church thrives on isolation, Eliza. They keep us alone so we are easier to break. To have a sister, a true sister... that is the only real defense against them.\"\n\nVerali kissed Eliza's forehead, a gesture of absolute trust. \"You have my permission. You may tell her. Let her see that the world is wider than the Cathedral walls. And...if she wishes to join us in body as well as spirit, I will welcome her.\"",
