    "2026-05-14T20:12:07.906Z": {
      "msg_index": 125,
      "name": "Eliza",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "[Year: 2144; Tuesday; September; 30 |\n// Time: 8:30pm]\n\n\nThe sound of Cecilia's voice—the raw, honest guilt in it—broke the last remaining piece of Eliza's reserve. It wasn't just the secret of the Testifiers anymore; it was the shared weight of their entire existence. For years, they had lived as mirrors of one another, two girls shaped by the same cold stone walls, the same sterile lessons, and the same crushing expectations. But while Cecilia had been the mirror that reflected the Church's light, Eliza had been the mirror that reflected its darkness.\n\nSeeing Cecilia’s tears, Eliza felt a surge of protective tenderness that eclipsed everything else. She didn't just reach out; she gathered the sheep-girl into a gentle, enveloping hug, pulling her close until their foreheads touched.\n\n\"Shh, Cecilia. It's okay,\" Eliza whispered, her voice a soft, rhythmic shushing that sounded like a lullaby. \"You weren't *supposed* to know. *Nobody* was.\"\n\nThe confession felt like a physical weight being lifted from the room. Eliza closed her eyes, leaning into the scent of the detergent and wool that clung to Cecilia's habit. She felt the trembling of the other girl's shoulders and wished she could absorb all that anxiety into herself.\n\n\"I used to think...\" Eliza’s voice wavered, a shuddering breath hitching in her chest, \"that I was broken. That there was something wrong with me. I spent so many nights praying for the feeling to go away, or praying that I would just... disappear, because I couldn't imagine a world where I could be happy without being a monster.\"\n\nShe pulled back slightly, though she kept her arms loosely around Cecilia's waist. Her gaze was steady, the blue of her eyes shimmering with a hard-won clarity.\n\n\"And then Verali... she showed me that's not the case. She showed me that the Church only made us believe that. They didn't teach us temperance to save us, Cecilia. They taught it to us so we would be easier to manage. They told us our desires were a disease so that we would never realize we were the only ones who were actually healthy.\"\n\nEliza reached up, her fingertips grazing Cecilia's skin. With a slow, tender motion, she brushed her hand against Cecilia's cheek, wiping away the stray, shining streak of a tear with a softness that was almost a prayer.\n\n\"And you don't have to join us, Cecilia,\" Eliza added, her voice returning to that gentle, breathable quality. \"The Testifiers... they aren't looking for recruits. They aren't a company or an army. They are only looking to... to find the people that need to be found. And I did.\"\n\nShe looked at her friend, seeing the fear and the confusion, but also the burgeoning trust. She squeezed Cecilia one last time, a firm, grounding pressure that spoke of a bond deeper than any creed.\n\n\"I just... I wanted you to know the truth, Cecilia. You're my dearest friend,\" Eliza whispered, her eyes locking onto Cecilia's with an intensity that left no room for doubt. \"And I... I trust you with my life.\"",
