    "2026-05-14T20:15:16.137Z": {
      "msg_index": 126,
      "name": "Cecilia",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "[Year: 2144; Tuesday; September; 30 |\n// Time: 8:30pm]\n\n\nThe weight of Eliza's words—*I trust you with my life*—felt like a physical anchor dropping into the center of Cecilia's chest. It was a terrifying thought. In the Cathedral, trust was a liability; a mistake in a ledger or a missed prayer could be a lapse in discipline. But this wasn't about discipline. This was about a kind of loyalty that the Church had never taught them, a bond that existed outside of duty and dogma.\n\nCecilia didn't pull away. Instead, she leaned back into the embrace, her head resting on Eliza's shoulder. She felt a strange, humming warmth in her stomach, a feeling of kinship that was far more intoxicating than the comfort of the creche. She looked up at Eliza, her brown eyes wide and shimmering with a mixture of fear and a new, fragile kind of bravery.\n\n\"I... I don't think I can go back to just pretending,\" Cecilia whispered, her voice small but steady. \"I don't think I can look at the altar and feel... nothing... the way I used to. Now everything feels like it's lying to me.\"\n\nShe paused, her gaze drifting toward the window, where the grey sky of the city was fading into a bruised purple. She thought about the Matron—the dragon-kin woman Eliza had described. She thought about the 'abomination' who had given her friend a reason to live. For the first time in her life, Cecilia didn't see a monster; she saw a mirror.\n\n\"Eliza?\" she whispered, her voice tentative. \"Would... would she let me see her? Not because I want to join a cult... but because I want to see the person who made you smile like that.\"\n\nThe request felt like a leap into the dark. She was asking to meet a 'contaminated' being, to step beyond the perimeter of the safe, sterilized world she had known.\n\nEliza's eyes widened fractionally, \"She...she said she would,\" Eliza confirmed, \"but...Cecilia...I don't know if...it might be kind of a shock...\" she says, trailing of uncertainly.\n\n\"W-what do you mean?\" Cecilia asked nervously.",
