      "name": "Eliza",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "[Year: 2144; Tuesday; September; 30 |\n// Time: 8:30pm]\n\n\nThe silence of the room seemed to amplify the sudden, frantic drumming of her heart. She looked at Cecilia—so innocent, so rooted in the modest, sheltered sensibilities of the creche—and a wave of protective hesitation washed over her. She tried to imagine Cecilia’s reaction to the loft, to the sheer, unvarnished carnality of the Testifier meetings.\n\nThe memories of her own afternoon flooded back: the smell of cured leather, the dim, flickering light, and the sight of bodies entwined in the shadows. In the Cathedral, the most intimate act was a whispered prayer or a clandestine touch in a dark corridor. In the loft, intimacy was the air they breathed.\n\nEliza’s face didn't just blush; it burned, a deep, crimson heat that climbed from her collar up to her hairline. She looked away, her gaze darting toward the blank, grey wall, her voice dropping to a breathless, frantic whisper.\n\n\"Oh... because... I mean... there's... people having...\" She stopped, the word *sex* feeling too blunt, too loud for the quiet of the dormitory. \"And it's... it's kind of... public, and...\"\n\nShe trailed off, her mind flashing back to her own position just a few hours prior. She had been buck-naked, her skin humming with the gold of Verali's seed, ravishing and being ravished with a feral intensity. There had been no curtains, no locked doors—only the thin, porous dividers of leather bales and the indifference of those who had already found their own truth. She had been entirely exposed, a raw nerve of desire in a room where such things were the only currency that mattered.\n\nThe thought that Cecilia—who still probably thought a hug was a daring display of affection—would be dropped into the center of that hedonistic, honest chaos made Eliza’s head spin. She could almost see Cecilia’s wide-eyed shock, the way she would likely clutch her habit to her chest in a panic.\n\n\"It's not... it's not like a church service,\" Eliza added, her voice trembling with a mix of embarrassment and a strange, secret pride. \"There is no modesty there, Cecilia. None at all. It's just... people. Being people. In every way they've been told they aren't allowed to be.\"\n\nShe looked back at her roommate, her blue eyes shimmering. \"I just... I don't want you to be frightened. I want you to see it and know that it's okay. But it's... it's a lot. It's a *lot* of everything.\"",
