      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "[Year: 2144; Tuesday; September; 30 |\n// Time: 8:30pm]\n\n\nThe word *public* echoed in Cecilia's mind, rattling like a loose stone in a jar. She stared at Eliza, her brown eyes blinking rapidly, her mouth slightly agape. She tried to visualize it—a room where people simply... *did* those things? Without a marriage license? Without the blessing of a priest? Without the walls of a bedroom and the heavy curtains of modesty?\n\nThe concept was almost physically repulsive to her; it felt like a violation of the natural order she had been taught. She imagined a chaotic, shouting mass of bodies, something out of the scandalous pamphlets the Wardens occasionally used to frighten the acolytes during their 'purity' seminars. The idea of someone seeing her in such a state—exposed, vulnerable, and driven by desire—made her skin prickle with a sudden, icy chill.\n\nBut beneath the shock, there was a spark. A tiny, flickering flame of curiosity that she couldn't extinguish.\n\n*What does it actually look like?* she wondered, her gaze drifting to the floor. *How can a person just... be... like that?*\n\nShe had spent twenty-one years being told that her body was a temple to be guarded, a vessel for the future, a thing to be handed over only when the Church deemed it appropriate. The idea that a place existed where that temple was simply... open... was scandalous. It was a crime. It was heresy.\n\nAnd it was, in a way that made her heart beat a little faster, intoxicating.\n\n\"Public...\" Cecilia whispered, the word tasting strange on her tongue. \"You mean... anyone can see? And they... they don't mind?\"\n\nShe felt a sudden, hot flash of embarrassment, her cheeks warming. She suddenly found herself very aware of the way her own habit felt against her skin—the heavy wool, the tight waistband. She imagined herself in that room, stripped of the black and white cloth, standing naked and shivering under the gaze of strangers. The thought made her feel small and fragile, but it also gave her a strange, dizzying sense of power. To be seen and not be judged. To be known and not be punished.\n\n\"I... I don't know if I could,\" she admitted, her voice small and shaky. \"I think I would just... I think I would faint.\"\n\nShe looked back at Eliza, her expression a mixture of horror and fascination. She felt like she was standing on the edge of a great, dark cliff, and Eliza was the one holding her hand, inviting her to jump.\n\n\"But...\" Cecilia added, her voice regaining a bit of its strength, a tiny, hesitant smile playing on her lips. \"If...if it's possible, I'd...I'd still like to meet...umm...your *friend*.\"\n\nShe leaned in, her voice dropping to a conspiratorial whisper, her curiosity finally outweighing her scandal. \"Is it... is it very loud? Do they... do they talk, or is it just... the noise of... *it*?\"",
