    "2026-05-15T07:48:50.307Z": {
      "msg_index": 143,
      "name": "Verali",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "[Year: 2144; Tuesday; October; 7\nTime: 12:00pm]\n\n\nVerali watched the two girls, her golden eyes softened by a profound, quiet warmth. She stood as a silent witness to the embrace, the heavy steam of the washhouse swirling around them like a curtain, shielding this small, private sanctuary from the rest of the industrial noise.\n\nShe had spent years facilitating the awakenings of others, guiding the broken and the suppressed through the fire of their own desires. She was accustomed to the dramatic breakdowns, the sudden screams of liberation, and the intense, often volatile energy of those newly awakened. But this was different. This was a quiet, aching tenderness.\n\nThe honesty of the sheep-girl had caught her off guard. Verali had expected Cecilia to ask about the \"monstrosity\" of her biology, or perhaps to shrink away in a fit of religious panic. She hadn't expected the girl to voice a grief born of a perceived failure in friendship. To hear Cecilia express terror not for herself, but for the fact that she hadn't noticed her friend's suffering, was a testament to a soul of rare, unvarnished purity.\n\nIn a city where everyone wore a mask—be it the mask of the pious acolyte, the mask of the greedy merchant, or the mask of the indifferent laborer—Cecilia had just stripped hers away. She had offered a vulnerability that was almost sacred.\n\nVerali felt a swell of genuine affection for the girl. It was a maternal pull, a protective instinct that flared up in the presence of such an earnest heart. Cecilia didn't value the liberation of the Testifiers because it was a political rebellion or a psychological curiosity; she valued it because she loved Eliza.\n\nSlowly, moving with the same careful deliberation she used when handling the most delicate linens, Verali reached forward. She placed a large, gentle hand on Cecilia's shoulder. Her palm was warm, her scales smooth, and her touch was light—a grounding weight that didn't overwhelm, but rather anchored.\n\n\"I see why Eliza loves you so,\" Verali said, her voice a low, melodic hum that seemed to resonate in the very bones of the room. The same warmth that Eliza found in the sanctuary was here, in the middle of a damp laundry, offered freely to a girl who had never known she deserved it.\n\nShe looked into Cecilia's brown eyes, her gaze steady and devoid of the predatory hunger the posters had promised. There was only a deep, shimmering recognition.\n\n\"You're a good-hearted person, Cecilia,\" Verali added softly, her thumb brushing the fabric of the girl's habit with a small, comforting gesture. \"A heart that feels the pain of another is a heart that is already awake, even if you don't yet know the name for it. I am... truly glad to know you.\"",
