    "2026-05-20T01:17:51.794Z": {
      "msg_index": 167,
      "name": "Father Gaspard",
      "is_user": false,
      "is_system": false,
      "mes": "[Year: 2144; Wednesday; October; 15\nTime: 7:30pm]\n\n\nFor a heartbeat, the world narrowed down to the sound of his own ragged, wheezing breath and the sight of two black-and-white habits standing in the grey slush of the Rookery. The vial of iridescent gold felt like a hot coal in his palm, a damning piece of evidence that could strip him of his rank, his status, and his sanctuary. He felt a sudden, visceral surge of panic; his stomach churned, and he felt as though his very internals were shrinking in terror.\n\nHis mouth remained agape, a small string of saliva clinging to his lip as he stared at them. *They saw. They saw it all.*\n\nThen, the instinct for survival—the same instinct that had allowed him to climb the ecclesiastical ladder by stepping on the necks of others—kicked in. With a jagged, forceful effort of will, he snapped his jaw shut. He straightened his spine, though he remained a bloated, sweating mass of a man, and tried to summon the air of a high-ranking official. There was no explaining this away; there was no theological justification for an Examiner buying black-market essence in a slum.\n\nThe only tool he had left was the only tool he had ever used: fear.\n\n\"I would... I would keep your mouths shut about this,\" he wheezed, his voice grating and thin, lacking its usual academic weight. He stepped forward, invading their space, his breath smelling of stale wine and nervous sweat. \"Do you not realize who I am? I am an *Examiner*! I could... I could have you publicly shamed in front of the entire congregation. I could have your names read from the pulpit as corrupted souls.\"\n\nHe sputtered, a bead of sweat rolling down his temple, his beady eyes darting between the two girls.\n\n\"I could put you on penance duties for the next decade,\" he continued, his tone shifting into a guttural snarl as he tried to regain the upper hand. \"Scrubbing the basement floors until your fingers bleed. Or...\" He stopped, his gaze locking onto Eliza. His eyes narrowed, focusing on her with a predatory intensity. \"Maybe... *re-education*.\"\n\nHe heard Cecilia gasp—a soft, terrified sound that usually fed his ego. But as he looked at Eliza, the expected reaction didn't come. There was no trembling. No downward cast of the eyes. No breathless apology.\n\nInstead, he was met with a hard, stony glare. Her blue eyes were cold, devoid of the submission he had spent years cultivating. They weren't the eyes of a frightened acolyte; they were the eyes of someone who looked at him and saw exactly what he was: a pathetic, frightened animal.\n\n*Why... why is she looking at me like that?* Gaspard wondered, a sudden chill running down his spine that had nothing to do with the rain. *Why... isn't she afraid?*\n\nThe silence from her was more unnerving than any accusation could have been. It was a void where her fear should have been, and for the first time in his career, Gaspard felt a flicker of genuine uncertainty. He took a subconscious step back, his heavy coat rustling.\n\n\"Not... not a word,\" he spat, his voice cracking. \"Or I'll make your lives hell, sisters.\"\n\nHe turned on his heel and stalked away, his gait uneven and hurried. As he retreated back toward the safer, cleaner districts, he could feel their eyes boring into his back. He didn't need to look back to know that it was Eliza's gaze that was the heaviest.\n\nEven as he vanished into the mist of the Rookery, Gaspard shivered. He had spent his life mastering the art of the mask, but for a moment, he felt as though Eliza had seen right through his, and the look in her eyes suggested that she no longer feared the man behind it.",
